WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:02.167
- She's a well-known business woman,

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.371
writer, and television personality.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.704
When her company went public

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:07.371
she became the first American

00:00:07.371 --> 00:00:09.905
self-made female billionaire.

00:00:09.905 --> 00:00:11.694
New York Magazine named her

00:00:11.694 --> 00:00:14.688
the definitive American woman of our time.

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:15.996
She's Martha Stewart

00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:19.579
and here are her Top
Ten Rules for Success.

00:00:21.659 --> 00:00:24.326
- Well I'm a very curious person

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.182
and that curiosity really is, I think,

00:00:28.182 --> 00:00:30.558
at the basis for all the kinds of things

00:00:30.558 --> 00:00:34.725
that I like to try and
experiment with, and attempt.

00:00:35.794 --> 00:00:38.438
And we have a good time doing it.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.658
It's not so much being driven

00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:44.652
as much as being interested
in a lot of different things.

00:00:44.652 --> 00:00:47.306
When you develop your business plan

00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:49.671
don't be afraid to write everything down.

00:00:49.671 --> 00:00:51.737
Everything that comes into your mind,

00:00:51.737 --> 00:00:54.917
because ultimately if you
have a good business plan,

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:57.203
well thought out, well designed,

00:00:57.203 --> 00:01:00.178
carried out for a year or two or three,

00:01:00.178 --> 00:01:04.393
you can start to follow that
plan in an orderly fashion.

00:01:04.393 --> 00:01:06.942
Doesn't always work,
it doesn't always work.

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:08.766
It doesn't always turn out

00:01:08.766 --> 00:01:10.638
the way you think it's going to turn out.

00:01:10.638 --> 00:01:14.284
You might stumble or
trip or fall in a gully.

00:01:14.284 --> 00:01:16.602
But if you have the plan you can get up

00:01:16.602 --> 00:01:18.727
and continue on your path.

00:01:18.727 --> 00:01:21.380
I really encourage them

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.125
if they have a great idea

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:25.375
to run with it.

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:28.257
Find ways to finance,

00:01:29.651 --> 00:01:31.063
find ways to build,

00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:33.563
find ways to market.

00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:36.345
Once you develop a large customer base,

00:01:36.345 --> 00:01:39.765
and we reach about a hundred
million people every month

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:42.214
with all our various
businesses, our books,

00:01:42.214 --> 00:01:44.386
our magazines, our television,

00:01:44.386 --> 00:01:47.620
and once you develop that
kind of close rapport

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.287
they have already a feeling that

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:54.551
I'm providing them with
things they need and want.

00:01:54.551 --> 00:01:56.644
So it's very important

00:01:56.644 --> 00:01:59.509
to engender trust with your customers.

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:02.213
If you disappoint them, I
mean, if you make something

00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:04.758
that falls apart, forget it.

00:02:04.758 --> 00:02:07.579
You don't get that customer back again.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:10.955
And all I want to do is
grow my customer base.

00:02:10.955 --> 00:02:14.470
I want to be where that
customer needs and wants me.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:17.692
Every business has, and
I don't like to think

00:02:17.692 --> 00:02:20.182
of things as obstacles all the time,

00:02:20.182 --> 00:02:23.740
I like to think of them
as challenges to be solved

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.225
and problems to be dealt with.

00:02:26.225 --> 00:02:27.740
When I started the business,

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.714
the Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia,

00:02:29.714 --> 00:02:32.881
our two words were inspire and inform.

00:02:34.149 --> 00:02:36.964
So you create the beautiful picture.

00:02:36.964 --> 00:02:38.936
You create the lifestyle

00:02:38.936 --> 00:02:42.112
that you think everybody would aspire to,

00:02:42.112 --> 00:02:44.667
and then you have to
tell them how to get it.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.290
So that's the teaching part.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.547
And to be that inspirer, that inspiration,

00:02:49.547 --> 00:02:51.010
you have to know a lot.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.423
You can't fake it.

00:02:52.423 --> 00:02:55.134
So I learn every single day.

00:02:55.134 --> 00:02:58.536
One of my mottoes is learn
something new every day.

00:02:58.536 --> 00:02:59.789
And I do.

00:02:59.789 --> 00:03:02.827
So it's all about informing yourself

00:03:02.827 --> 00:03:05.086
so that you can be a good teacher.

00:03:05.086 --> 00:03:07.752
- Have you ever cried in business
ever, your entire career?

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:08.615
- Cried?
- Yes.

00:03:08.615 --> 00:03:10.387
- No, I refuse.

00:03:10.387 --> 00:03:12.748
- How do you, well, I
think it's interesting--

00:03:12.748 --> 00:03:14.682
- I cry, but I don't cry in business.

00:03:14.682 --> 00:03:15.515
- You don't cry in business.

00:03:15.515 --> 00:03:18.370
- No, I don't think business
is worth crying over.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.901
I think you have to, again,
concentrate on business,

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.466
you can build your business,

00:03:24.466 --> 00:03:26.939
you can help others build businesses,

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:28.878
and it's business.

00:03:28.878 --> 00:03:30.624
It's not about emotion.

00:03:30.624 --> 00:03:32.702
It's about really going for it.

00:03:32.702 --> 00:03:33.603
You can be passionate.

00:03:33.603 --> 00:03:37.656
That's the only emotion
I allow in my business.

00:03:37.656 --> 00:03:40.725
I have always said ever
since I started working

00:03:40.725 --> 00:03:42.558
that I am my customer.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:45.486
I want to appeal to me.

00:03:45.486 --> 00:03:47.151
What's missing in my life?

00:03:47.151 --> 00:03:49.322
What void can I fill

00:03:49.322 --> 00:03:54.188
that will fill the voids for
everybody that's like me?

00:03:54.188 --> 00:03:55.563
And my mother would always say,

00:03:55.563 --> 00:03:57.630
"Nobody's like you, Martha! Forget it!"

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.959
And I always said, "Mother,
I am like everybody else."

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:03.998
And you know, I have
chickens, I have a garden,

00:04:03.998 --> 00:04:06.409
I scrub the floors, I vacuum my house.

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:08.239
I'm just like everybody else.

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:10.331
And so she finally got to understand

00:04:10.331 --> 00:04:11.504
what I was talking about,

00:04:11.504 --> 00:04:15.962
because I always want to
please me with what we do.

00:04:15.962 --> 00:04:17.303
Do I want to buy it?

00:04:17.303 --> 00:04:18.661
Do I need it?

00:04:18.661 --> 00:04:20.509
So it's the need and the want.

